    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (76.28) stands as our premier offensive anchor. Facing a weak arm in Bratt (xERA 5.90), **Wood** benefits from an elite xwOBA profile and a high-leverage spot in the lineup, making him the highest-projected efficiency play on the board. **Brice Turang** (72.70) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) are also locked in as strong starts; both profit significantly from plus-matchups against right-handed pitchers, with **Turang**\u2019s speed profile and favorable SP skill differential providing the necessary juice to secure his slot. **Austin Riley** (72.42) rounds out our elite tier, boosted by a massive +16% park factor that compensates for his lower spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Isaac Paredes**, who landed at 52.31\u2014just outside the optimal lineup. While his dynamic platoon edge against a righty is notable, he ultimately failed to displace **Gabriel Moreno** or **Zach McKinstry** due to the lineup ambiguity surrounding his #3 spot. We are also keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki** (45.82); despite his low score, he remains in the lineup, though he faces a significant hurdle today against the elite Paul Skenes. His inclusion is a strategic gamble that his high batting position will generate counting stats, but his score is suppressed heavily by Skenes' dominant skill profile.\n\nWe are consciously navigating risks elsewhere in the roster. **Jose Caballero** (51.18) remains active despite a tough matchup against a lefty; we are banking on his stolen base potential despite the presence of an elite catcher who threatens his success rate. Conversely, we have benched **Dalton Rushing** (38.41) and **Cole Young** (40.15) entirely, as both fell below our 40-point efficiency floor. With the scarcity of steals as our primary focus, we are willing to stomach the volatility of players like **Corbin Carroll** (65.34)\u2014whose 100% SB probability keeps him in the starting nine\u2014rather than chasing the marginal floor of non-base-stealing bench pieces.",
